{
 "title": "Enums y match",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "Un **`enum`** enumera las opciones (**variantes**) que puede tomar un valor. Para mirar un valor de un enum se usa **`match`**. Su característica más importante: el compilador comprueba que se traten **todos los casos**. Si olvidas una variante, el código no compila."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "enum TrafficLight:",
    "    Red",
    "    Yellow",
    "    Green",
    "",
    "fn action(light: TrafficLight):",
    "    match light:",
    "        TrafficLight.Red:",
    "            print(\"Stop!\")",
    "        TrafficLight.Yellow:",
    "            print(\"Get ready...\")",
    "        TrafficLight.Green:",
    "            print(\"Go!\")",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    action(TrafficLight.Red)",
    "    action(TrafficLight.Green)"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "Stop!",
    "Go!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "Si no quieres escribirlas todas, `_:` recoge todo lo demás."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "enum TrafficLight:",
    "    Red",
    "    Yellow",
    "    Green",
    "",
    "fn is_stop(light: TrafficLight) -> bool:",
    "    match light:",
    "        TrafficLight.Red:",
    "            return true",
    "        _:",
    "            return false",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    print(is_stop(TrafficLight.Red), is_stop(TrafficLight.Yellow))"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "true false"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "exercise",
   "id": "c06-l01-x1",
   "prompt": "Para el enum `Direction` (`North`, `South`, `East`, `West`), escribe `name(d)`: imprime su propio nombre (`north`, `south`...). Llámala con `West`.",
   "starter": [
    "enum Direction:",
    "    North",
    "    South",
    "    East",
    "    West",
    "",
    "fn name(d: Direction):",
    "    match d:",
    "        Direction.North:",
    "            print(\"north\")",
    "        _:",
    "            print(\"?\")",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    name(Direction.West)"
   ],
   "solution": [
    "enum Direction:",
    "    North",
    "    South",
    "    East",
    "    West",
    "",
    "fn name(d: Direction):",
    "    match d:",
    "        Direction.North:",
    "            print(\"north\")",
    "        Direction.South:",
    "            print(\"south\")",
    "        Direction.East:",
    "            print(\"east\")",
    "        Direction.West:",
    "            print(\"west\")",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    name(Direction.West)"
   ],
   "hint": "Escribe una rama para cada variante; deja fuera el `_`.",
   "expected": [
    "west"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "quiz",
   "id": "c06-l01-q1",
   "q": "¿Qué ocurre si olvidas una variante dentro de `match`?",
   "options": [
    "Falla en tiempo de ejecución",
    "El código no compila",
    "Se salta en silencio"
   ],
   "answer": 1,
   "why": "`match` es exhaustivo: un caso que falta es un error de compilación."
  }
 ]
}
